Suggests: gamepadtool, joystick
Description: native port of Pokémon: Let's Go, Eevee! / Pikachu! (static recompilation)
 A native Linux port of the Nintendo Switch games Pokémon: Let's Go, Eevee! and
 Pokémon: Let's Go, Pikachu!, made by static recompilation: the games' ARM64 code
 is translated into C and compiled for the computer, and a runtime stands in for
 the Switch (system services, NVN graphics on Vulkan, audio, controllers). It is
 not an emulator.
 .
 The package carries the runtime, the start screen and the tools the start screen
 needs to recompile the game on the player's own machine (the game code
 generator, the C compiler and the headers the game code is built against). The
 game's own files are not included: you need your own legally obtained copy,
 extracted (the exefs and romfs folders).
 .
 Everything the program writes (game files, saves, settings, shader caches, the
 log) stays in $XDG_DATA_HOME/letsgo-recomp (~/.local/share/letsgo-recomp).
 .
 Not affiliated with Nintendo, The Pokémon Company, Game Freak or Creatures.
